      "content": "You raise a valid concern that many archivists face when imposing structured systems on inherently fluid collections. Using these categories as fixed, rigid codes can indeed sometimes flatten the narrative context of non-linear or mixed-media manuscripts, making the \"disorder\" feel artificial rather than descriptive. Professional practice often addresses this by adopting an element-based classification approach (such as the EBA) where each unique object is indexed by its own attributes rather than forced into a single sequence, thus preserving the manuscript's individuality while remaining accessible.",
